#519 sgirandomcolour -- PRE-TABLE CHECK for KILL TABLE 4 (the CLASS CLOSURE).
Opus measuring seat.  Written BEFORE table 4's first build; its mtime is the proof of order.

WHAT CHANGED SINCE TABLE 3
  regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py only.  src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c is UNTOUCHED (md5
  6e2c6873, unchanged since 2026-09-10 04:26).  This is a DETECTOR diff, not a product diff.
  59 rows -> 77: twenty-two added, four deleted.

  Smoke against the fix BEFORE this file was written: 77/77, every new row green, on a clone
  verified PART1 CLEAN / PART2 FRESH.  That is a dry run, not table 4; table 4 is the frozen
  measurement.

================================================================ 0.  THE ENUMERATION AND ITS BOUND

The floor question is asked of the SHIPPED COMPOSITE, so it is asked over the guarded store's
COMPLETE free input set rather than over a list of mutant forms.  The guarded body is one
statement and reads exactly four lvalues:

    cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, tileptr + ofs, buf, bufdepth, MEM_WRITE, ...)

    bufdepth  <- (mode>>8)&3                             FREE    {1,2,4,8}      CLOSED (table 3)
    tileptr   <- tlb_mode (array), tile_nr (element)     tlb_mode {0,1,2,4}     CLOSED (table 3)
    ofs       <- x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode                DERIVED
    buf       <- color_mode (arm), *color (value)

THE BOUND, and it is the whole reason this is closable rather than #392: tile_nr, tile_nr_x,
tile_nr_y, xofs and ofs are NOT independent axes.  Each is a pure function of
(x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode), and the latter two are already closed.  So "close every derived
coordinate" IS "close the pair (x, y)" -- two free variables.  The complete free input set is

        { bufdepth, tlb_mode, color_mode, *color, x, y }

of which table 3 closed the first two.  Table 4 closes the other four.  THE SET IS FINITE AND
READ OFF THE FUNCTION; it cannot grow by argument.

WHY A CLASS CLOSURE AND NOT ANOTHER CELL.  Three consecutive passes found ONE shape -- a decline
conditioned on an input the rows hold at a single value.  Pass 1/2 of table 3: bufdepth (M13),
tlb_mode (M14).  Pass 2 of this round: tile index (M30/M31/M32), tiled y (M33), nibble (M28),
foreground value (M37) -- six mutants at 59/59, each measured writing uninitialised host stack
into guest memory (artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260911/).  The rule forbids buying a cell.

================================================================ 1.  SIBLING PARITY

The diff de-fatalises nothing new -- it adds rows.  The sibling comparison that applies is
between the FOUR closed axes, and it is where the asymmetry was:

    axis         body's own partition                   driven before      driven now
    bufdepth     {1,2,4,8} (the shift domain)           4 of 4             4 of 4
    tlb_mode     {0,1,2,4} reachable to the store       4 of 4             4 of 4
    color_mode   5 labels; 12 values reach `default'    5 labels, 2 values 5 labels, 12 values
    *color       no body test; one value held           1                  2
    x, y         {0}, within-tile, crossing-tile        (0,0) + one linear (0,0) + 4 tiled

ASYMMETRY FOUND AND CLOSED: three axes were closed over a DOMAIN and three over a single point.
No axis is now driven at fewer than two distinct classes.

================================================================ 2.  CLAIM -> ROW

Every added sentence asserting an observable consequence, mapped to the row that observes it.
The trigger is SEMANTIC (does this sentence assert something a row could observe?), not a verb list.

  "ten declined nibbles ... announce ONCE"                        -> nib ann
  "an RGBA PUT drawn in a SECOND colour lands whole"              -> nib accept alt
  "closes the *color axis for free"                               -> nib 40..e0 (all ten at FG_ALT)
  "lands in THIS cell's own tile at its own offset"               -> xy acc c1..c4 (4 distinct addrs)
  "no cell silently collapsed onto [tile 0]"                      -> xy anchor t0
  "four declined PUTs across four tiles announce ONCE, and the
   four ACCEPTS are silent"                                       -> xy ann (cumulative == 1
                                                                      covers BOTH halves)
  "x IS 132 AND NOT 128 ... xofs [would stay] 0"                  -> xy acc c1 lands at ofs 16,
                                                                      which is the observable
  "y IS 129 AND NOT 128 ... 128 masks to zero"                    -> xy acc c4 lands at ofs 528
                                                                      (= 512*1 + 16), so y is 1
  "C4 IS THE JOINT CELL"                                          -> xy dec c4
  "the cross-PUT latch ... is still pinned by `once'"             -> once (retained row)

NO ADDED SENTENCE IS WITHOUT A ROW.  Two claims are deliberately NOT rowed and are stated as
disclosures instead, in the contract: a predicate enumerating the driven cell set by value, and
coordinate-joined-to-width/label mutants.

================================================================ 3.  GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD

Guard (the predicate that decides the decline): `color_mode', a local derived from `mode'.
Guarded BODY: cpu->memory_rw(..., tileptr + ofs, buf, bufdepth, MEM_WRITE, ...).
Body-read lvalues: tileptr, ofs, buf, bufdepth, cpu->mem.

*** TABLE 3's ENTRY FOR THIS SECTION WAS WRONG AND THE ERROR IS WHY TABLE 4 EXISTS. ***
It concluded: "`color_mode' is written nowhere the body reads.  So a decline conditioned on
color_mode is invisible to any body-side oracle and is coverage debt, not floor."

That applied a DIFFERENT test from the one it applied to tlb_mode two lines above.  For tlb_mode
it used the 2026-09-09 flow test (tlb_mode flows into tileptr, a body-read lvalue -> FLOOR AXIS).
For color_mode it asked whether color_mode is ITSELF read by the body.  Under the flow test,
color_mode selects among four arms EVERY ONE OF WHICH WRITES `buf' -- the store's DATA operand --
so it flows, and the same section's own line says so ("buf <- written by the four supported arms").

  The disposition on M28 survived anyway, for a narrower and correct reason: the body's own tests
  partition color_mode into FIVE LABELS and all five were driven, so M28 sliced WITHIN a label,
  which the 2026-09-04 ruling files as clause (e).

  THE COST WAS ELSEWHERE.  The same mis-stated test also excluded `tile_nr' -- and tile_nr flows
  into `tileptr', the ADDRESS operand, as the INDEX of the very array tlb_mode selects
  (`tileptr = d->re_tlb_a[tile_nr] << 16').  It passes the flow test unambiguously.  `#100' in
  this same function already calls tile_nr "guest-derived" and added a bound for it.

WHERE GUARD AND BODY DISAGREE, restated correctly:
  `buf' is written by the four supported arms and NOT by the default arm.  The DISAGREEING STATE
  is "the store runs with buf unassigned" -- which is what every permitting mutant produces, and
  what pass 2 measured six times (0x70630000, 0x6368696e, 0x706300fe, 0x706300d6, 0x706300c3).
  `0x6368696e' is ASCII "chin": host stack text reaching guest-visible memory.

================================================================ 4.  CHANNEL -- per NEW row, the mutant it kills and the observable that differs

  nib 40..e0 (10)   M28_permit_othernibbles and any nibble-set predicate
                    -> word at phys 0x10000 != paint.  MEASURED in pass 2: nib60 read 0x706300c3.
  nib 40..e0 (10)   M37_fgvalue and any *color predicate
                    -> same channel; these ten are the only declined cells drawn in FG_ALT.
                       MEASURED in pass 2 (FGAXIS.out): 0x706300fe at fg 0x12345678.
  nib accept alt    a mutant declining a SUPPORTED type, or one keyed to FG_VAL on the accept
                    side -> word != 0x5a3c691e.  Non-vacuous: M8_declineall is in table 4.
  nib ann           a latch that re-fires per nibble -> count != 1.  M5_nolatch is in table 4.
  xy dec c1         M30/M31/M32 (tile_nr, tile_nr_x), `ofs == 0', `xofs == 0'
                    -> word at 0xa0020010 != paint.  MEASURED in pass 2: t1 read 0x70630000.
  xy dec c2         M33 (`linear || y == 0') and any post-mask y predicate
                    -> word at 0xa0010200 != paint.  MEASURED in pass 2: ty1 read 0x706300d6.
  xy dec c3         a `tile_nr_y == 0' predicate -> word at 0xa0040000 != paint.
  xy dec c4         the PAIRWISE DISJUNCTIONS -- `tile_nr==0 || y==0', `tile_nr_x==0 ||
                    tile_nr_y==0', `xofs==0 || y==0' -- which every other cell satisfies.
  xy acc c1..c4     a decode that sends one cell's PUT to another cell's tile, and the
                    de-escalation ACCEPT side -> each reads its own distinct address; the four
                    addresses are 0x20010 / 0x10200 / 0x40000 / 0x50210, so a collapse is visible.
  xy anchor t0      a cell collapsing onto tile 0 while its own cell still looks untouched
                    -> word at 0xa0010000 != paint.
  xy ann            an announce on an ACCEPT, or a latch re-firing across tiles -> count != 1.

VACUOUS-BY-CONSTRUCTION AUDIT: no new row is survive-only, and none rests on a channel that
cannot vary under its named mutant -- every one of the eleven channels above is a READBACK or a
COUNT, and six of them were MEASURED to vary in pass 2 before this table was designed.

  *** THE ONE I HAD TO FIX BY ENUMERATING, recorded because it nearly shipped. ***  My pass-2
  control used x = 128.  At x = 128 `x % tilewidth_in_pixels' is 0, so xofs stays 0 and
  `if (xofs == 0) ok = 0;' would have swept table 4 clean even WITH a tile_nr row present.
  x = 132 makes tile_nr_x and xofs non-zero in one cell.  Found by enumerating the derived set
  against the cells, not by running another table.

================================================================ 5.  THE DELETIONS, AND THEIR WARRANT

Four rows deleted: `tA ann cum', `tB ann cum', `tC ann cum', `lin ann cum'.

  MEASURED over table 3's 26 mutants, each of their kill sets is {M1,M11,M5,M7} -- a STRICT
  SUBSET of the matching `ann1' row's {M1,M11,M5,M7,M9,M10,M16,M17}.  They carried no kill of
  their own.  Rows are owed PER ENUMERATED MUTANT, and two rows no enumerated mutant
  distinguishes collapse into one.

  NO MUTANT LOSES ITS ONLY KILL, checked before deleting rather than after: M5_nolatch keeps
  {once, tA/tB/tC ann1}; M7_silent keeps its announce-text reds; M1 and M11 keep 32 reds each.

  WHAT THEY PINNED IS STILL PINNED.  `ann cum' was the only whole-transcript announce count in
  its window, so it alone covered the `rpt' cell's announce.  `once' is also a whole-transcript
  count (two declined PUTs in one process, cumulative == 1) and is RETAINED, so cross-PUT
  latching keeps an oracle.  The two new blocks add `nib ann' and `xy ann', both cumulative.

  `tA/tB/tC silent' are KEPT although their table-3 kill sets also nest inside `ann1's.  They
  pin a DIFFERENT property -- that an ACCEPTED type announces nothing -- which no table-3 mutant
  isolates.  Rather than judge it, table 4 BUILDS the discriminator: M38_acceptannounce adds an
  announce to the RGBA arm, which should red `silent' and NOT `ann1'.  If it does, the rows are
  justified by measurement; if it does not, they are deletable and I will say so.

  `ycrcb x4y1' is KEPT and is now DISCHARGED: its own comment claims it kills `if (ok || x)' and
  `|| y', table 3 built neither, and its kill set there was a strict subset of `lin ycrcb d1'.
  Pass 2 built M34/M35/M36 (`|| ofs', `|| x', `|| y') and each scored 58/59 with that row as the
  SOLE red.  The claim is measured, not asserted.

